Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables, columns, and how they will be used

• orders.orderid : joins orders to order_details.  
• orders.customerid : identifies the buyer and lets us aggregate by customer.  
• orders.orderdate : lets us keep only the 1998 orders (WHERE substr(orderdate,1,4)=‘1998’).  

• order_details.unitprice : line‑item price.  
• order_details.quantity : multiply by unitprice to get the line amount.  
• order_details.discount : to be ignored (“excluding any discounts”).  
• order_details.orderid : joins back to orders.  

• customergroupthreshold.rangebottom / rangetop : numeric limits that define each spending band.  
• customergroupthreshold.groupname : label of the spending band.  

• customers.customerid / customers.companyname (optional) : readable name of the customer if needed.

Main conditions that will be applied  
• substr(orders.orderdate,1,4) = '1998'  – just the 1998 orders.  
• JOIN customergroupthreshold ON customer_total BETWEEN rangebottom AND rangetop – to classify each customer.  

------------------------------------------------------------------
Exploratory & build‑up queries  
(The ten queries below progress from very simple inspection to the final result.  Each query is limited to 20 rows where that makes sense.)

```sql
-- 1. List the different years that appear in the orders table
SELECT DISTINCT substr(orderdate,1,4) AS order_year
FROM orders
ORDER BY order_year;
```

```sql
-- 2. Sample of orders placed in 1998
SELECT orderid,
       customerid,
       orderdate
FROM orders
WHERE substr(orderdate,1,4) = '1998'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Distinct customers that placed at least one order in 1998
SELECT DISTINCT customerid
FROM orders
WHERE substr(orderdate,1,4) = '1998'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Line‑item information for 1998 orders, including extended price
SELECT od.orderid,
       od.productid,
       od.unitprice,
       od.quantity,
       (od.unitprice * od.quantity) AS line_total
FROM order_details AS od
JOIN orders        AS o  ON o.orderid = od.orderid
WHERE substr(o.orderdate,1,4) = '1998'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Total amount of each 1998 order (no discount applied)
SELECT od.orderid,
       SUM(od.unitprice * od.quantity) AS order_total
FROM order_details AS od
JOIN orders        AS o  ON o.orderid = od.orderid
WHERE substr(o.orderdate,1,4) = '1998'
GROUP BY od.orderid
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Total 1998 spending per customer
SELECT o.customerid,
       SUM(od.unitprice * od.quantity) AS customer_total
FROM orders        AS o
JOIN order_details AS od ON od.orderid = o.orderid
WHERE substr(o.orderdate,1,4) = '1998'
GROUP BY o.customerid
ORDER BY customer_total DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Display the spending‑threshold table
SELECT *
FROM customergroupthreshold
ORDER BY rangebottom;
```

```sql
-- 8. Classify each 1998 customer into a spending group
WITH customer_spend AS (
  SELECT o.customerid,
         SUM(od.unitprice * od.quantity) AS customer_total
  FROM orders        AS o
  JOIN order_details AS od ON od.orderid = o.orderid
  WHERE substr(o.orderdate,1,4) = '1998'
  GROUP BY o.customerid
)
SELECT cs.customerid,
       cs.customer_total,
       cgt.groupname
FROM customer_spend         AS cs
JOIN customergroupthreshold AS cgt
  ON cs.customer_total BETWEEN cgt.rangebottom AND cgt.rangetop
ORDER BY cs.customer_total DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. How many 1998 customers fall into each spending group
WITH customer_spend AS (
  SELECT o.customerid,
         SUM(od.unitprice * od.quantity) AS customer_total
  FROM orders        AS o
  JOIN order_details AS od ON od.orderid = o.orderid
  WHERE substr(o.orderdate,1,4) = '1998'
  GROUP BY o.customerid
),
classified AS (
  SELECT cs.customerid,
         cgt.groupname
  FROM customer_spend         AS cs
  JOIN customergroupthreshold AS cgt
    ON cs.customer_total BETWEEN cgt.rangebottom AND cgt.rangetop
)
SELECT groupname,
       COUNT(*) AS customer_count
FROM classified
GROUP BY groupname
ORDER BY customer_count DESC;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final output: customer count and percentage share of each group
WITH customer_spend AS (
  SELECT o.customerid,
         SUM(od.unitprice * od.quantity) AS customer_total
  FROM orders        AS o
  JOIN order_details AS od ON od.orderid = o.orderid
  WHERE substr(o.orderdate,1,4) = '1998'
  GROUP BY o.customerid
),
classified AS (
  SELECT cs.customerid,
         cgt.groupname
  FROM customer_spend         AS cs
  JOIN customergroupthreshold AS cgt
    ON cs.customer_total BETWEEN cgt.rangebottom AND cgt.rangetop
),
totals AS (
  SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_customers
  FROM classified
)
SELECT c.groupname,
       COUNT(*)                                   AS customer_count,
       ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(*) / t.total_customers, 2) AS percentage_of_total
FROM classified AS c
CROSS JOIN totals AS t
GROUP BY c.groupname
ORDER BY customer_count DESC;
```

